## Checking actor views

`actor_view_snapshot` renders an activated, visible actor view in your run browser and returns what the user sees as accessible text. Use it to check a mini-app's interface; the server resolves the address, so never open a view{{#if (available "browser_navigate")}} with `browser_navigate`{{/if}} yourself.
Call the actor's functions first, then take the snapshot to see whether the interface shows the same state. The browser stays on the view{{#if (available "browser_take_screenshot")}}: `browser_take_screenshot` captures it{{/if}}{{#if (available "browser_click" "browser_type" "browser_check")}}, and `browser_click`, `browser_type` and `browser_check` operate it with `target.frame: "iframe"`{{/if}}.
